INT. MINOR LEAGUE BASEBALL CLUBHOUSE - NIGHT

Lockers. Bats in racks. A cooler of sports drink. Rain drums on a tin roof.

The Millbrook Herons sit in a loose half-circle. MANAGER LEONARD "SKIP" CUELLAR (60s, thick mustache) stands before them. Around him: PITCHER DARIUS WHELAN (20s), CATCHER BEATRIZ "BEA" FONSECA (30s), SHORTSTOP KENJI NAKASHIMA (20s), and TRAINER OLUWASEUN "SEUN" ADEBAYO (40s).

SKIP
Good game, fellas. Good game.

DARIUS
We lost eleven to two, Skip.

SKIP
Did we? I didn't notice.

BEA
You were in the dugout, Skip. You noticed.

SKIP
I notice everything, Bea. That's why I'm manager.

KENJI
You called a bunt with two outs.

SKIP
It was a tactical bunt.

SEUN
It was a tactical disaster, boss.

SKIP
Seun, you're a trainer.

SEUN
And I trained for this.

DARIUS
Skip, are we still in the standings?

SKIP
Technically.

BEA
Technically how?

SKIP
Technically, there are eight teams, and you can't be lower than eighth.

KENJI
We're eighth.

SKIP
See? Technically alive.

DARIUS
Skip, I walked nine batters.

SKIP
Nine is a nice number.

BEA
Skip, I've never seen you this calm.

SKIP
That's because I've got news, Bea.

SEUN
Good news?

SKIP
Franchise is moving. Sold to a company in Tulsa. Last game's Sunday.

Nobody speaks. The rain gets louder.

DARIUS
Seriously?

SKIP
I wouldn't kid, Darius. Not about this.

KENJI
When did you know?

SKIP
Since March. Didn't want to spoil the season.

BEA
Spoil it? Skip --

SKIP
Bea, wait. I'm proud of every one of you. Win or lose.

SEUN
(quietly)
We mostly lost.

SKIP
We mostly lost beautifully, Seun.
